#==========================================================================================================================================
# Architecture
#==========================================================================================================================================
    32-bit machine: registers, immediates and addresses are 32 bits (4 bytes), big endian.
    The address bus has 28 lines: addresses are masked to 0x0FFFFFFF (256 MiB address space).

    Moves:  mov  / omov  / movo   32 bits (dword)
            movw / omovw / movwo  16 bits (word)
            movb / omovb / movbo   8 bits (byte)
        Moving 16 or 8 bits into a whole register zero-extends the value.
        omov* / mov*o offsets: <imm> (8-bit), dword <imm> (32-bit, "word <imm>" also accepted), <register>

    Registers:
        System:  IP SP FP RV PP FL ACC
        General: R1 .. R20
        Special: S1 S2 OF (reg(0x07), reg(0x08), reg(0x09))
        16-bit halves of the general registers: R1L .. R20L (bits 0-15), R1H .. R20H (bits 16-31)
            Reading a half gives it zero-extended; writing a half changes only that half (any instruction
            taking a register accepts a half, e.g.  movw R1H, 0x1234   mov R2L, R3H   inc R4L).
        Encoding: 1 byte, register index in bits 0-5, view in bits 6-7 (0x00 whole, 0x40 low, 0x80 high).
            IP 0x00, SP 0x01, FP 0x02, RV 0x03, PP 0x04, FL 0x05, ACC 0x06, S1 0x07, S2 0x08, OF 0x09,
            R1..R20 0x0A..0x1D

    Stack: grows down from the last 4 bytes of the RAM; push / pop / call / ret move 32-bit values.
        Stack frame (above FP, 4 bytes each): StackFrameSize, FP, IP, ACC, PP, R20..R1, ArgCount, args



